        "id": "0a806520-e847-49c5-afaf-7e68989af7e2",
        "kind": "problem",
        "theorem_name": "OAI.PiExponent.DeterminantContradiction.piEventualLowerBound_of_interpolation_and_analytic_aggregate",
        "theorem_title": "The conditional interpolation and analytic determinant argument for pi",
        "formal_statement": "theorem OAI.PiExponent.DeterminantContradiction.piEventualLowerBound_of_interpolation_and_analytic_aggregate\r\n    (hgeometry : GlobalInterpolationStatement) (hanalytic : AnalyticAggregateStatement) :\r\n    PiEventualLowerBound := by\n  sorry\n",
        "natural_language_statement": "Assume the global interpolation statement and the analytic aggregate statement for the original fixed admissible data. Then, for every real $\\nu>2$, there is an integer $Q\\ge2$ such that every $p\\in\\mathbb Z$ and $q\\in\\mathbb N$ with $q\\ge Q$ satisfy\n\n$$q^{-\\nu}\\le\\left|\\pi-\\frac pq\\right|.$$\n\nThis is the conditional conclusion of the source determinant contradiction, with the original quantified interpolation and analytic hypotheses.",
        "definitions": "import Definitions.Def_OAI_PiExponent_ApproximationDefinitions\nimport Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_DeterminantContradiction_CoreData\n\nopen OAI.PiExponent OAI.PiExponent.DeterminantContradiction\n\n",
        "source": "https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/NumberTheory/PiExponent/Approximation/DeterminantContradiction.lean#L167-L180",
